{
  "_comment": [
    "Pico y placa restriction rules by department.",
    "",
    "Structure:",
    "  departments.<dept_code>.rules[] — ordered list of rule blocks.",
    "  The first rule whose date range contains the check date is used.",
    "  A rule without effective_from/effective_until applies to all dates.",
    "",
    "Logic types:",
    "  'parity'  — based on day-of-month odd/even.",
    "              restrictions.odd  = digits blocked on odd days  (1,3,5,...)",
    "              restrictions.even = digits blocked on even days (2,4,6,...)",
    "  'weekday' — based on ISO weekday name (Monday–Friday).",
    "              restrictions.<DayName> = list of digits blocked that day.",
    "              Absent weekday key = no restriction that day.",
    "              Saturday and Sunday are never restricted (all plates may circulate).",
    "",
    "Digit values are the last character of the license plate ('0'–'9' as strings).",
    "",
    "To update a rotating schedule:",
    "  1. Set effective_until on the current rule to the last day of its validity.",
    "  2. Add a new rule block with effective_from set to the first day of the new period.",
    "  3. Fill in the new restrictions.",
    "",
    "Departments absent from this file have no restriction (all plates pass through)."
  ],

